  "testDataStatus": "AppendixQNationalPosConditionCodeOracle implements bounded, code/format-recognition-only checks for all four fixed-position sub-fields (Terminal Class, Presentation Type, Security Condition, Terminal Type) plus the full 21-entry Terminal Type catalog, and two additional field-level rules from Table ID 030's own attribute description outside the Q-1 through Q-7 pages: conditional requiredness (Appendix I-19) and the Visa CAVV trigger for Terminal Type 25/26 (Appendix I-19). The eWIC attended self-checkout case (section 10.5.5.6) of flow consistency is also now assertable given a TransactionContext. General cross-field flow consistency with Prompt Code/entry mode/lifecycle remains REVIEW_REQUIRED because Appendix Q does not itself state that broader rule.",
  "remaining": ["Resolve general channel-specific POS condition cross-field consistency with Prompt Code, POS Entry Mode, and transaction lifecycle beyond the eWIC self-checkout case (requires SME input beyond Appendix Q's own text).", "Element 203 \"Safekey Data\" (Segment 123, NFC payment tokenization) ties SafeKey AEVV/AESK mandatory/optional status to Terminal Type 25/26/27; this is that element's own rule and belongs to a future Segment 123/Element 203 training effort, not Appendix Q's validator.", "Appendix I's Visa-India recurring-payment rules require Terminal Type '25' together with CAVV Cryptogram and recurring-transaction-indicator conditions; this is a narrow Visa-India recurring-payment business rule, not Appendix Q's own general text, and is deferred to a future Visa-recurring-payment-specific training effort."]
